{"pages": [{"page": 1, "text": "====================================================================================================\n\nCITY GENERAL HOSPITAL & OPD CLINIC\n\nDr. A. Sen, MBBS, MD (General Medicine) | Reg. No: WB-24901\n\nAddress: 45/2, Acharya Jagadish Chandra Bose Road, Kolkata\n\n====================================================================================================\n\nPatient Name: Ramesh Verma Age/Sex: 38 / Male\n\nDate: 12/10/2026 Weight: 72 kg\n\nVITAL SIGNS:\n\n- Temperature: 101.4^○F (Intermittent)\n\n- Blood Pressure: 122/82 mmHg\n\n- Pulse Rate: 92 bpm\n\nCHIEF COMPLAINTS:\n\n1. Moderate frontal headache lasting for the past 5 days.\n\n2. Low-grade fever with mild chills lasting for the past 3 days.\n\nCLINICAL IMPRESSION / PROVISIONAL DIAGNOSIS:\n\n- Acute febrile illness with tension-type headache (Rule out viral etiology / seasonal infection).\n\nRx (MEDICATIONS):\n\n1. Tab. Paracetamol 650 mg\n\n- 1 tablet orally, SOS (maximum every 6 hours after food if temperature > 100^○F or severe headache)\n\n- Duration: 3 days\n\n2. Cap. Pantoprazole 40 mg\n\n---\n\n- 1 capsule orally, once daily (empty stomach in the morning)\n\n- Duration: 5 days\n\n## 3. ORS (Oral Rehydration Salts)\n\n- 1 packet mixed in 1 liter of water, sip throughout the day\n\nINVESTIGATIONS ADVISED:\n\n- Complete Blood Count (CBC) with ESR\n\n- Dengue NS1 Antigen & IgM/IgG\n\n- Malaria Parasite (ICT)\n\nADVICE:\n\n- Strict physical rest and adequate oral hydration (at least 3 liters/day).\n\n- Monitor and maintain temperature chart.\n\n- Review with lab reports after 48 hours or immediately if breathlessness or high persistent fever develops.\n\nSignature:\n\nDr. A. Sen, MD"}, {"page": 2, "text": "{\"page_num\":1,\"image_width\":2481,\"image_height\":3508,\"created_at\":\"2026-10-12T09:35:54.376096Z\",\"blocks\":[{\"block_id\":\"p1-b1\",\"coordinates\":{\"x1\":296,\"y1\":310,\"x2\":1770,\"y2\":342},\"bbox_norm\":[0.11930673115679162,0.08836944127708096,0.7134